module ScaleEngraver

@ UserVisible = false @
@ SystemModule = true @
@ Author = "Benjamin Boeck" @

# ScaleEngraver: engraves rulers and dials with ONE command each.
#
#   EngraveRuler X=10 Y=10 Z=0 length=100
#   EngraveDial  X=60 Y=60 Z=0 radius=30
#
# Everything except the position and the size has a default, so a scale needs one line. The defaults are
# defined once in millimetres and are converted automatically when the control is set to inch:
#
#   tickLength    6 mm     length of the LONGEST tick (all other ticks are derived from it)
#   factor        0.7      every finer tick level is 70 percent as long as the level before it
#   depth         0.1 mm   engraving depth of ticks, line and numbers (positive = how deep)
#   labelHeight   half the tick length, at least 2.5 mm
#   feedHeight    1 mm     height above Z where the movement starts with the plunge feed
#   infeedZ       depth    maximum depth per cut (one cut by default)
#
# The calling program selects the tool, sets Rpm, the feeds (SetFeedTechnology plunge= finishing=), the retract height
# (SafeZHeightForWorkpiece) and Spindle On/Off. X, Y and Z give the position like in the Line command; Z is the height of
# the surface, the depth is measured from it. Every engraving starts with PrePositioning: up to the safe height, over the
# start, down to the feed height.
# The engine (parameter structures, geometry as data) is the module ScaleEngraverCore.

using Base
using ScaleEngraverCore
import Math
import AxisSystem

@doc: The kind of ruler. Millimeter: ticks every 1 mm, a medium tick every 5 mm, a long tick with a number every
10 mm (the numbers are millimetres). Centimeter: the same ticks, the numbers are centimetres (1, 2, 3 ...).
Inch: an inch ruler built by halving - inch, 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16 - each level with a shorter tick, big numbers for
the inches and small fractions beside the longer ticks. @
export enumeration ScaleKind (Millimeter, Centimeter, Inch)

@doc: The kind of dial. Degrees: a full circle 0 to 360, a number every 30 degrees, a tick every 5 degrees.
Percent: a full circle 0 to 100, a number every 10. Gauge: 0 to 100 over 270 degrees, from the lower left over
the top to the lower right. Protractor: a half circle 0 to 180 with ticks and horizontal numbers inside. @
export enumeration DialKind (Degrees, Percent, Gauge, Protractor)

@doc: How the numbers of a dial are turned. Tangential: the numbers follow the circle, their top points away from the centre.
Radial: the numbers run along the radius. Horizontal: the numbers are not turned. @
export enumeration NumberOrientation (Tangential, Radial, Horizontal)

# Millimetres per unit of the control: 1 when the control is metric, 25.4 when it is set to inch.
program MillimetersPerUnit returns number
    system = AxisSystem::MeasuringSystem
    if system == AxisSystem::MeasuringSystems.Imperial
        return 25.4
    endif
    return 1
endprogram

# A readable distance between two numbered ticks for a custom value range: 1, 2 or 5 times a power of ten,
# so that the range has roughly ten numbers.
program NiceMajorStep (span:number) returns number
    raw = Math::Abs(span) / 10
    if raw <= 0
        return 1
    endif
    magnitude = Math::Pow(10, Math::Floor(Math::Log10(raw)))
    mantissa = raw / magnitude
    niceStep = 10 * magnitude
    if mantissa <= 5.0001
        niceStep = 5 * magnitude
    endif
    if mantissa <= 2.0001
        niceStep = 2 * magnitude
    endif
    if mantissa <= 1.0001
        niceStep = magnitude
    endif
    return niceStep
endprogram

# How many parts a long-tick distance is divided into: a step of 2 (2, 20, 0.2 ...) gets 4 parts, others 10.
program NiceMinorDivisions (distance:number) returns number
    magnitude = Math::Pow(10, Math::Floor(Math::Log10(distance)))
    mantissa = distance / magnitude
    if mantissa > 1.9999 and mantissa < 2.0001
        return 4
    endif
    return 10
endprogram

@doc: ![](images/header_EngraveRuler.png)

Engraves a ruler with one command. Mandatory: where the ruler starts (X, Y, Z) and how long it is. The
ticks, the numbers, the depth and the heights have defaults (see the module description); the kind is
Millimeter when the control is metric and Inch when it is set to inch. Example: EngraveRuler X=10 Y=10 Z=0 length=100 @
export program EngraveRuler (
    X:number
        @doc: X of the start of the ruler (the zero tick).@
    Y:number
        @doc: Y of the start of the ruler.@
    Z:number
        @doc: ![](images/referenceZ.png)

Z of the surface of the part at the ruler. All depths are measured from this height.@
    length:number
        @doc: ![](images/scaleLength.png)

Length of the ruler in the unit of the control (mm, or inch when the control is set to inch).@
    optional kind:ScaleKind
        @doc: Millimeter, Centimeter or Inch. Default: Millimeter on a metric control, Inch on an inch control.@
    optional valueStart:number
        @doc: The value at the start of the ruler. Together with valueEnd this makes your own scale, for example a ruler that shows 20 at its start. Default: 0.@
    optional valueEnd:number
        @doc: The value at the end of the ruler. The ruler shows the values from valueStart to valueEnd over its length, with a number every 1, 2 or 5 times a power of ten (about ten numbers); change that with majorStep.
Default: valueStart plus the length (in mm, cm or inch, depending on the kind).@
    optional majorStep:number
        @doc: ![](images/majorStep.png)

Value distance between two long ticks (the ticks with a number). Default: 10 (Millimeter), 1 (Centimeter), 1 (Inch), or chosen by itself when you set valueEnd.@
    optional tickLength:number
        @doc: ![](images/tickLength.png)

Length of the longest tick. All other ticks are derived from it with the factor. Default: 6 mm.@
    optional factor:number
        @doc: ![](images/tickStyles.png)

Every finer tick level is this much as long as the level before it: 0.7 gives 100 / 70 / 49 percent of the longest
tick (millimetre ruler) and 100 / 70 / 49 / 34 / 24 percent (inch ruler down to 1/16). Default: 0.7.@
    optional depth:number
        @doc: ![](images/depth.png)

Engraving depth of ticks, line and numbers, measured from Z (positive = how deep). Default: 0.1 mm.@
    optional angle:number
        @doc: ![](images/rotationAngle.png)

Direction of the ruler in degrees: 0 = to the right (+X), 90 = upwards (+Y). Default: 0.@
    optional below:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/side_negative.png)

true = ticks and numbers on the right-hand side of the direction (below a ruler running to the right). Default: false = left-hand side (above).@
    optional labelHeight:number
        @doc: ![](images/labelHeight.png)

Height of the numbers. Default: half the tick length, at least 2.5 mm.@
    optional numbers:boolean
        @doc: false = no numbers, only ticks. Default: true.@
    optional skipFirst:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/skipFirstTick.png)

Leave out the first tick and its number, for example where the ruler starts on the edge of the part. Default: false.@
    optional skipLast:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/skipLastTick.png)

Leave out the last tick and its number. Default: false.@
    optional baseline:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/baselineDepth.png)

true = also engrave the line along the ticks. Default: true.@
    optional levels:number
        @doc: ![](images/levels.png)

Inch ruler: how often the inch is halved. 3 = down to 1/8, 4 = 1/16, 5 = 1/32. Default: 4.@
    optional fractionLevel:number
        @doc: ![](images/fractionLabelLevel.png)

Inch ruler: fractions get a number down to this level. 0 = none, 1 = halves, 2 = also quarters, 3 = also eighths. Default: 2.@
    optional infeedZ:number
        @doc: ![](images/infeedZ.png)

Maximum depth per cut. The depth divided by infeedZ gives the number of cuts; they alternate in direction without lifting the tool. Default: the depth (one cut).@
    optional feedHeight:number
        @doc: ![](images/feedHeight.png)

Height above Z where the movement starts with the plunge feed. The tool gets there with PrePositioning, via the safe height set with SafeZHeightForWorkpiece. Default: 1 mm.@
    )
    mm = MillimetersPerUnit
    if not kind hasvalue
        kind = ScaleKind.Millimeter
        if mm > 1
            kind = ScaleKind.Inch
        endif
    endif
    if not tickLength hasvalue
        tickLength = 6 / mm
    endif
    if not factor hasvalue
        factor = 0.7
    endif
    if not depth hasvalue
        depth = 0.1 / mm
    endif
    if not angle hasvalue
        angle = 0
    endif
    if not below hasvalue
        below = false
    endif
    if not labelHeight hasvalue
        labelHeight = Math::Max(2.5, tickLength * mm * 0.5) / mm
    endif
    if not numbers hasvalue
        numbers = true
    endif
    if not skipFirst hasvalue
        skipFirst = false
    endif
    if not skipLast hasvalue
        skipLast = false
    endif
    if not baseline hasvalue
        baseline = true
    endif
    if not levels hasvalue
        levels = 4
    endif
    if not fractionLevel hasvalue
        fractionLevel = 2
    endif
    if not infeedZ hasvalue
        infeedZ = 0
    endif
    if not feedHeight hasvalue
        feedHeight = 1 / mm
    endif

    heights = NewEngraveHeights(referenceZ=Z feedHeight=feedHeight infeedZ=infeedZ)
    side = TickSide.Positive
    if below
        side = TickSide.Negative
    endif
    lineDepth = 0
    if baseline
        lineDepth = depth
    endif
    # without numbers: the first number is skipped and the label interval is never reached again
    labelEvery = 1
    if not numbers
        labelEvery = 1000000
    endif

    # the values of the scale: by default the length of the ruler in the unit of the kind
    if not valueStart hasvalue
        valueStart = 0
    endif
    customRange = valueEnd hasvalue
    if not valueEnd hasvalue
        valueEnd = valueStart + length * mm
        if kind == ScaleKind.Centimeter
            valueEnd = valueStart + length * mm / 10
        endif
        if kind == ScaleKind.Inch
            valueEnd = valueStart + length * mm / 25.4
        endif
    endif

    if kind == ScaleKind.Inch
        levels = Math::Max(1, Math::Min(6, Math::Round(levels)))
        styles:TickStyle[] = {}
        for k from 0 to levels
            levelStyle:TickStyle = {tickLength * Math::Pow(factor, k), depth}
            append levelStyle to styles
        endfor
        unitNumbers = NewLabelSettings(labelHeight=labelHeight labelDepth=depth labelEvery=labelEvery skipFirstLabel=not numbers)
        if not numbers
            fractionLevel = 0
        endif
        inchRuler = NewFractionScale(originX=X originY=Y scaleLength=length valueStart=valueStart valueEnd=valueEnd unitLabel=unitNumbers levels=levels tickStyles=styles fractionLabelLevel=fractionLevel rotationAngle=angle side=side skipFirstTick=skipFirst skipLastTick=skipLast baselineDepth=lineDepth)
        EngraveFractionScale scale=inchRuler heights=heights
    else
        if not majorStep hasvalue
            majorStep = 10
            if kind == ScaleKind.Centimeter
                majorStep = 1
            endif
            if customRange
                majorStep = NiceMajorStep(span=valueEnd - valueStart)
            endif
        endif
        minorParts = NiceMinorDivisions(distance=majorStep)
        mediumAt = 5
        if minorParts == 4
            mediumAt = 2
        endif
        major = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength tickDepth=depth)
        medium = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength * factor tickDepth=depth)
        minor = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength * factor * factor tickDepth=depth)
        division = NewScaleDivision(valueStart=valueStart valueEnd=valueEnd majorStep=majorStep minorDivisions=minorParts mediumEvery=mediumAt skipFirstTick=skipFirst skipLastTick=skipLast)
        numberStyle = NewLabelSettings(labelHeight=labelHeight labelDepth=depth labelEvery=labelEvery skipFirstLabel=not numbers)
        ruler = NewLinearScale(originX=X originY=Y scaleLength=length division=division majorTick=major minorTick=minor mediumTick=medium labelFormat=numberStyle rotationAngle=angle side=side baselineDepth=lineDepth)
        EngraveLinearScale scale=ruler heights=heights
    endif
endprogram

@doc: ![](images/header_EngraveDial.png)

Engraves a dial (clock face, gauge, protractor) with one command. Mandatory: the centre (X, Y, Z) and the radius
of the scale circle. The kind sets range, steps, sweep and number orientation; everything can be overridden.
Example: EngraveDial X=60 Y=60 Z=0 radius=30 @
export program EngraveDial (
    X:number
        @doc: X of the centre of the dial.@
    Y:number
        @doc: Y of the centre of the dial.@
    Z:number
        @doc: ![](images/referenceZ.png)

Z of the surface of the part at the dial. All depths are measured from this height.@
    radius:number
        @doc: ![](images/radius.png)

Radius of the scale circle in the unit of the control. The ticks start on this circle.@
    optional kind:DialKind
        @doc: Degrees, Percent, Gauge or Protractor. Default: Degrees.@
    optional tickLength:number
        @doc: ![](images/tickLength.png)

Length of the longest tick. The others are derived with the factor. Default: 20 percent of the radius, at most 6 mm.@
    optional factor:number
        @doc: ![](images/tickStyles.png)

Every finer tick level is this much as long as the level before it. Default: 0.7.@
    optional depth:number
        @doc: ![](images/depth.png)

Engraving depth of ticks, line and numbers, measured from Z (positive = how deep). Default: 0.1 mm.@
    optional labelHeight:number
        @doc: ![](images/labelHeight.png)

Height of the numbers. Default: half the tick length, at least 2.5 mm.@
    optional numbers:boolean
        @doc: false = no numbers, only ticks. Default: true.@
    optional valueStart:number
        @doc: The value at the start angle. Together with valueEnd this makes your own scale, for example a gauge from 20 to 80. Default: 0.@
    optional valueEnd:number
        @doc: The value at the end angle. The dial shows the values from valueStart to valueEnd over its sweep. Default: from the kind (360, 100, 100, 180).@
    optional majorStep:number
        @doc: ![](images/majorStep.png)

Value distance between two long ticks (the ticks with a number). Default: from the kind (30, 10, 10, 10), or chosen by itself when you set valueEnd.@
    optional startAngle:number
        @doc: ![](images/startAngle.png)

Angle of the first value in degrees: 0 = to the right, 90 = 12 o'clock, counter-clockwise. Default: from the kind.@
    optional endAngle:number
        @doc: ![](images/endAngle.png)

Angle of the last value in degrees. Smaller than the start angle runs clockwise. Default: from the kind.@
    optional inside:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/side_negative.png)

true = ticks and numbers inside the circle. Default: from the kind (only the protractor is inside).@
    optional orientation:NumberOrientation
        @doc: ![](images/orientation_tangential.png)

How the numbers are turned: Tangential follows the circle, Radial runs along the radius, Horizontal is not turned.
Default: from the kind.@
    optional skipFirst:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/skipFirstTick.png)

Leave out the first tick and its number. Default: false.@
    optional skipLast:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/skipLastTick.png)

Leave out the last tick and its number. Default: false.@
    optional baseline:boolean
        @doc: ![](images/baselineDepth.png)

true = also engrave the circle line (arc). Default: true.@
    optional infeedZ:number
        @doc: ![](images/infeedZ.png)

Maximum depth per cut. The depth divided by infeedZ gives the number of cuts; they alternate in direction without lifting the tool. Default: the depth (one cut).@
    optional feedHeight:number
        @doc: ![](images/feedHeight.png)

Height above Z where the movement starts with the plunge feed. The tool gets there with PrePositioning, via the safe height set with SafeZHeightForWorkpiece. Default: 1 mm.@
    )
    mm = MillimetersPerUnit
    if not kind hasvalue
        kind = DialKind.Degrees
    endif

    # the kind sets the defaults of range, steps, sweep, side and number orientation
    kindEnd = 360
    kindStep = 30
    kindMinor = 6
    kindMedium = 0
    kindStart = 90
    kindStop = -270
    kindInside = false
    kindOrientation = NumberOrientation.Tangential
    kindNumberEvery = 1
    if kind == DialKind.Percent
        kindEnd = 100
        kindStep = 10
        kindMinor = 5
    endif
    if kind == DialKind.Gauge
        kindEnd = 100
        kindStep = 10
        kindMinor = 5
        kindStart = 225
        kindStop = -45
        kindNumberEvery = 2
    endif
    if kind == DialKind.Protractor
        kindEnd = 180
        kindStep = 10
        kindMinor = 10
        kindMedium = 5
        kindStart = 180
        kindStop = 0
        kindInside = true
        kindOrientation = NumberOrientation.Horizontal
        kindNumberEvery = 2
    endif

    if not valueStart hasvalue
        valueStart = 0
    endif
    customRange = valueEnd hasvalue
    if not valueEnd hasvalue
        valueEnd = kindEnd
    endif
    if not majorStep hasvalue
        majorStep = kindStep
        if customRange
            majorStep = NiceMajorStep(span=valueEnd - valueStart)
            kindMinor = NiceMinorDivisions(distance=majorStep)
            kindMedium = 0
            if kindMinor == 4
                kindMedium = 2
            endif
        endif
    endif
    if not startAngle hasvalue
        startAngle = kindStart
    endif
    if not endAngle hasvalue
        endAngle = kindStop
        # a full circle keeps running one turn clockwise when only the start angle is moved
        if startAngle <> kindStart and kindStop == kindStart - 360
            endAngle = startAngle - 360
        endif
    endif
    if not inside hasvalue
        inside = kindInside
    endif
    if not orientation hasvalue
        orientation = kindOrientation
    endif
    if not tickLength hasvalue
        tickLength = Math::Min(6, radius * mm * 0.2) / mm
    endif
    if not factor hasvalue
        factor = 0.7
    endif
    if not depth hasvalue
        depth = 0.1 / mm
    endif
    if not labelHeight hasvalue
        labelHeight = Math::Max(2.5, tickLength * mm * 0.5) / mm
    endif
    if not numbers hasvalue
        numbers = true
    endif
    if not skipFirst hasvalue
        skipFirst = false
    endif
    if not skipLast hasvalue
        skipLast = false
    endif
    if not baseline hasvalue
        baseline = true
    endif
    if not infeedZ hasvalue
        infeedZ = 0
    endif
    if not feedHeight hasvalue
        feedHeight = 1 / mm
    endif

    heights = NewEngraveHeights(referenceZ=Z feedHeight=feedHeight infeedZ=infeedZ)
    side = TickSide.Positive
    if inside
        side = TickSide.Negative
    endif
    lineDepth = 0
    if baseline
        lineDepth = depth
    endif
    coreOrientation = LabelOrientation.Tangential
    if orientation == NumberOrientation.Radial
        coreOrientation = LabelOrientation.Radial
    endif
    if orientation == NumberOrientation.Horizontal
        coreOrientation = LabelOrientation.Horizontal
    endif
    labelEvery = kindNumberEvery
    if not numbers
        labelEvery = 1000000
    endif

    major = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength tickDepth=depth)
    medium = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength * factor tickDepth=depth)
    minor = NewTickStyle(tickLength=tickLength * factor * factor tickDepth=depth)
    division = NewScaleDivision(valueStart=valueStart valueEnd=valueEnd majorStep=majorStep minorDivisions=kindMinor mediumEvery=kindMedium skipFirstTick=skipFirst skipLastTick=skipLast)
    numberStyle = NewLabelSettings(labelHeight=labelHeight labelDepth=depth labelEvery=labelEvery skipFirstLabel=not numbers)
    dial = NewCircularScale(centerX=X centerY=Y radius=radius division=division majorTick=major minorTick=minor mediumTick=medium labelFormat=numberStyle startAngle=startAngle endAngle=endAngle side=side orientation=coreOrientation baselineDepth=lineDepth)
    EngraveCircularScale scale=dial heights=heights
endprogram

end
